jobs.description:
We are a local English school deeply rooted in the Hamburg community. Since our founding in 1999, we’ve been committed to providing high-quality, professional English education. Locally owned and managed, we pride ourselves on our friendly and familial atmosphere.

We strive to make classes engaging and educational, by playing games, reading books and singing songs with the children. We mostly teach groups of six to eight children, offering classes in kindergartens across Hamburg, at our school in Lokstedt, and in private homes. Our goal is to familiarise children with English from an early age while still keeping lessons fun.

We are always on the lookout for new teachers to help us provide quality education across Hamburg. So if you are an enthusiastic and motivated English teacher, then we’d love to hear from you!

Your focus points

- Delivering high quality, learner-centric instruction;
- Recognising and addressing the specific needs of each learner, helping them achieve their personal goals;
- Fostering a positive and supportive learning environment;
- Providing a variety of activities to address different learning styles;
- Encouraging learners to share ideas and ask questions;
- Assisting young children in their learning and play and maintaining a safe, stimulating environment;
- Using imagination and creativity while planning and implementing learning activities;
- Making learning English fun.

You have

- Experience working with young children (including your own);
- A lively, flexible and adaptable teaching style;
- A friendly and confident manner;
- Creative skills and ideas for planning practical and interesting lessons;
- The desire and comfort to incorporate singing and music into lessons;
- A teaching qualification such as CELTA, TEFL or TESOL; or
- Experience as an ESL or EFL teacher;
- A passion for education and the English language;
- A love of play.

Then we have just the right job for you! We offer:

- Regular classes across Hamburg and at our academy in Lokstedt;
- A creative and friendly working environment;
- Flexible working hours;
- The cosy and supportive atmosphere of a locally-owned and locally managed business;
- The freedom to develop and structure your own classes;
- A wide range of teaching materials;
- Professional advice from our management team.

We look forward to hearing from you!

Click here to open the application form! (https://lollipops.de/forms/application/)

LERNIUS GmbH / LolliPops

E-Mail: application@lernius.de (application@lernius.de) 

For a quicker application process

Time is precious and to shorten the processing time of your application we would appreciate a short (max. 1minute!) introduction video of yourself where you show us a glimpse of your teaching style. (e.g. tell a story, sing a song or read a book etc) – Thank you!
